'' MIR lowering for procedures, scalar locals, arithmetic, IF, FOR, WHILE, DO and
'' EXIT. The golden file is the point: docs/plan/13 makes emitted IR a test surface,
'' so the text is asserted on directly and any change to it has to be deliberate.
''
'' Two structural properties are worth naming because they are easy to lose:
'' every alloca is in the entry block, and every block ends in exactly one
'' terminator -- both are verifier rules, and the verifier runs here.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/basic.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-NOT: <NO TERMINATOR>
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/basic.out
